From 5d20d44403cc1c803a730e0777e5cbf1cef730d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:12:53 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Cache-first bound: work below cache leaves a cache reader
 connections

A cache reader runs in its own lane and never pipelines behind downloads, so
under a saturating download it waited for a connection's whole pipeline to
drain, then stacked its entire read-ahead on that one connection, sharing the
provider with every download connection. With the playback bound on, cache
reads counted as background work and could not take the connections playback
left free at all. Cache readers waited seconds between segments.

Now an active or lingering cache reader bounds the work below it like playback
does: that work leaves it the connections it holds plus four, up to three
quarters of the limit, and from 16 connections up it keeps a second headroom
slot so a cache reader's first read finds an idle connection. A cache request
pipelines on its own connection only up to the pipeline depth; past that it
waits, which makes work below it yield and spreads the read-ahead.
